The release looks at every thread with units that waits without time and leaves each where it was.
A thread whose account reached a tick would wait on the spare or spent queue for good;
a thread with units that waits without time reaches a tick no earlier than the release.

Caught-by: fuzz fuzz-pmp8 fuzz-rp2350 fuzz-smp2 fuzz-work test qemu-replay
Report: a thread waits on another queue than its account says
Report: a thread's account reaches a tick before the release

diff --git a/kernel/sched.c b/kernel/sched.c
--- a/kernel/sched.c
+++ b/kernel/sched.c
@@ -396,7 +396,7 @@ static void release(uint32_t c)
         LOOP_BOUND(TIME_UNITS);
         struct thread *t = unit_first(first + i);
         if (t != NULL && (t->queue == QUEUE_SPARE || t->queue == QUEUE_SPENT)) {
-            thread_settle(t);
+            (void)t;
         }
     }
 }
